\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Physical PVB profiles and divergence in the singular limit $w_0 \to 0$. (a) Annular radial intensity profiles $I(r)$ with locked radius $R_0 = 1.0\,\text  {mm}$ across topological charges $\ell =1$ to $10$. (b) Topological radial shift $\Delta R_\ell - \Delta R_0 \approx \ell ^2 w_0^2 / (8 R_0)$, matching exact numerical extremum locations ($\approx 20\,\mu \text  {m}$ for $\ell =4$, relative shift $\le 3\%$). (c) Three physical divergence pillars as $w_0 / R_0 \to 0$: transverse wavevector variance $\langle k_\perp ^2 \rangle \sim 1/w_0^2$, peak irradiance $I_{\max } \propto 1/w_0$, and beam propagation quality factor degradation $M^2 \sim R_0 / w_0$. (d) Paraxial angular spectrum and optical bandwidth cutoff $K_{\max } = k \cdot \text  {NA}$.}}{22}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
